   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Making someone do something",
     "texto": [
      "To say that someone makes another person do something, or lets them do it, use **-게 하다**: 가다 → **가게 하다** (to make (someone) go), 먹다 → **먹게 하다** (to make (someone) eat), 공부하다 → **공부하게 하다** (to make (someone) study).",
      "선생님은 우리에게 노래를 **듣게 해요** = the teacher makes us listen to songs."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference from the causative",
     "texto": [
      "**-게 하다** works with any verb, even those without a causative. The causative (previous lesson) is a fixed form of the verb.",
      "공부하게 해요 = makes (someone) study. 공부시켜요 = makes (someone) study (fixed verb)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
